Description
This crashes inside jax.jit:
import jax
import jax.numpy as jnp

def f(x):
    try:
        return jnp.unique(x)
    except jax.errors.ConcretizationTypeError | jax.errors.NonConcreteBooleanIndexError:
        return x

x = jnp.arange(10)
f(x)  # OK
jax.jit(f)(x)  # TypeError: catching classes that do not inherit from BaseException is not allowed
Workaround
    try:
        return jnp.unique(x)
    except (jax.errors.ConcretizationTypeError, jax.errors.NonConcreteBooleanIndexError):
        return x
System info (python version, jaxlib version, accelerator, etc.)
Python 3.10
JAX 0.4.35

Currently, jax.vmap errors on an empty tree:
$ py -c "import jax; print(jax.vmap(lambda x: {'key': x})([None, {}, [], ()]))"
ValueError: vmap wrapped function must be passed at least one argument containing an array, got empty *args=([None, {}, [], ()],) and **kwargs={}
The error can be avoided by setting axis_size to some value:
$ py -c "import jax; print(jax.vmap(lambda x: {'key': x}, axis_size=0)([None, {}, [], ()]))"
{'key': [None, {}, [], ()]}
$ py -c "import jax; print(jax.vmap(lambda x: {'key': x}, axis_size=1)([None, {}, [], ()]))"
{'key': [None, {}, [], ()]}
$ py -c "import jax; print(jax.vmap(lambda x: {'key': x}, axis_size=2)([None, {}, [], ()]))"
{'key': [None, {}, [], ()]}
It would make for a better user experience if jax.vmap worked on empty trees by default, out of the box, without having to manually set axis_size to some value.
